      "tr": "`ports.setdefault(src, set()).add(port)` tekrarları kendiliğinden atar.",
      "en": "`ports.setdefault(src, set()).add(port)` drops repeats by itself."
    },
    {
      "tr": "Sonra `len(seen) >= limit` olanları adres sırasıyla döndür.",
      "en": "Then return those with `len(seen) >= limit` in address order."
    },
    {
      "tr": "Çözümün tamamı:\n\n```python\nimport ipaddress\n\n\ndef suspects(log, limit):\n    ports = {}\n    for src, port in log:\n        ports.setdefault(src, set()).add(port)\n    found = [src for src, seen in ports.items() if len(seen) >= limit]\n    return sorted(found, key=ipaddress.ip_address)\n\nlog = [[\"198.51.100.10\", p] for p in range(20, 30)]\nlog += [[\"198.51.100.9\", p] for p in [22, 80, 443]]\nlog += [[\"192.168.1.10\", 443], [\"192.168.1.10\", 443]]\nprint(suspects(log, 10))\nprint(suspects(log, 3))\n```",
      "en": "The full solution:\n\n```python\nimport ipaddress\n\n\ndef suspects(log, limit):\n    ports = {}\n    for src, port in log:\n        ports.setdefault(src, set()).add(port)\n    found = [src for src, seen in ports.items() if len(seen) >= limit]\n    return sorted(found, key=ipaddress.ip_address)\n\nlog = [[\"198.51.100.10\", p] for p in range(20, 30)]\nlog += [[\"198.51.100.9\", p] for p in [22, 80, 443]]\nlog += [[\"192.168.1.10\", 443], [\"192.168.1.10\", 443]]\nprint(suspects(log, 10))\nprint(suspects(log, 3))\n```"
    }
